WEBVTT

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:02.601
How do you grow a person on your team?

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:05.667
Same way a good trainer grows you.

00:00:05.687 --> 00:00:08.223
They add 5 KILOS to the bar.

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:10.563
Maybe 10. Never 20.

00:00:10.313 --> 00:00:12.920
Enough that you feel it.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.085
Light enough that you RECOVER.

00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:17.491
Careers work the same way.

00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:22.316
The job is to keep finding the GOLDILOCKS load —

00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:25.349
the extra weight that's just right.

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:29.652
In a career, the extra weight comes in a few shapes:

00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:32.452
a harder technical problem,

00:00:32.202 --> 00:00:34.502
a RISKIER deployment,

00:00:34.252 --> 00:00:36.227
one more team to align,

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:40.520
or a project that runs MONTHS instead of weeks.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.950
Get the load right, and the person steps out of their comfort zone,

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.502
learns something new —

00:00:47.252 --> 00:00:51.688
and still feels neither STRESSED nor DEFEATED.

00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:53.464
Here's one from my team.

00:00:53.214 --> 00:00:57.410
One engineer could already coordinate inside our team,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.678
and with the team next door.

00:00:59.428 --> 00:01:04.003
The next level: aligning teams BEYOND our org.

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:08.064
So I set it up on purpose, as a stretch.

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:11.791
ONE extra team beyond our org. Just one.

00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:13.835
He aligned them beautifully.

00:01:13.585 --> 00:01:17.734
And from that point on, his range grew —

00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:19.324
and so did my trust.

00:01:19.074 --> 00:01:24.044
Next time something like this comes up, it's HIS.

00:01:23.794 --> 00:01:26.924
So here is my working theory:

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:29.973
People grow at the GOLDILOCKS load.

00:01:29.723 --> 00:01:33.663
A little more than what they can carry today.

00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:36.856
Light enough to RECOVER from.

00:01:36.606 --> 00:01:43.372
And finding that weight — again and again, one person at a time —

00:01:43.122 --> 00:01:45.150
that's most of the MANAGER'S JOB.
